### UC12 – Cancel Tour By Guide (happy path, with a reason)
# Prerequisite: a SCHEDULED or RUNNING guide tour. Copy its id below.
# Cancels the tour AND every cancellable booking attached to it, in one transaction.
# The response reports how many bookings went with it.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/guide-tours/{{guideTourId}}/cancel
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Severe weather warning"
}

### UC12 – Cancel Tour By Guide (happy path, no reason)
# The body is optional, as is the reason. A bare POST cancels the tour.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/guide-tours/{{guideTourId}}/cancel

### UC12 – A client-supplied cancellation time is ignored (200)
# There is no cancelledAt field on the request: the driver reads ClockPort
# (architecture.definition.md section 8.1). The same instant is passed to the booking side,
# so both contexts record one moment. The 1999 date below has no effect.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/guide-tours/{{guideTourId}}/cancel
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cancelledAt": "1999-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "reason": "Trying to backdate the cancellation"
}

### UC12 – Error: blank reason (400)
# Cancelling without a reason is allowed; cancelling with an empty one is not.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/guide-tours/{{guideTourId}}/cancel
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "   "
}

### UC12 – Error: malformed guideTourId (400)
# UUID.fromString raises IllegalArgumentException in the driver, mapped to 400.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/guide-tours/not-a-uuid/cancel

### UC12 – Error: guide tour not found (404)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/guide-tours/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/cancel

### UC12 – Error: tour already FINISHED or CANCELLED (409)
# Prerequisite: complete a tour (UC11) or cancel it once, then retry.
# The guide side is NOT idempotent, unlike the booking side: this is the deliberate act at
# the top of the chain, so a 409 tells the guide the tour was already called off.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/guide-tours/{{guideTourId}}/cancel

### UC12 – Error: booking side rejected the cancellation (502)
# Not reproducible locally without breaking the booking context on purpose: the booking
# inport is in-process, so it only fails if MarkBookingCancelledByGuideDriver throws.
# 502 rather than 500 because the guide's request was well-formed and the tour was
# cancellable — the failure is downstream and retryable. The tour cancellation is rolled
# back, asserted by CancelTourByGuideRollbackIT rather than by this request.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/guide-tours/{{guideTourId}}/cancel
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Would roll back if the booking side failed"
}
